id: pm-yhle2e
title: "GH-1146/1147: external blockers remain stale and validation recommends deleting them"
description: "GitHub issues #1146 and #1147 show that accepted external blocked_by locators are never re-resolved, remain permanently blocking with unknown status, and are then misclassified by validate as dangling local corruption with a destructive --unset blocked_by hint."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:graph","area:sdk",context-integrity,external-references,github-1146,github-1147
created_at: "2026-08-28T21:25:57.770Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-29T12:50:14.108Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-29T12:50:13.597Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-29T12:50:13.597Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: External references are typed and preserved rather than counted as dangling local ids; A public resolver extension point returns bounded status title source and checked-at evidence without core GitHub coupling; Unresolved external blockers expose age and resolver availability while resolved blockers can trigger the existing auto-unblock transition; Validation never recommends destructive deletion for a well-formed external locator; SDK CLI MCP health next validate and temporary-workspace acceptance remain contract-parity with exact coverage
parent: pm-33cw
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub issues #1146 and #1147
severity: high
environment: pm 2026.8.28 in fresh local workspaces plus a long-lived cross-repository blocker
repro_steps: Block an item on a GitHub issue URL; close the remote issue; observe pm next still counting an unknown blocker and pm validate classifying the locator as dangling with an unset hint.
resolution: External endpoint collection now applies graph-target normalization to scalar and structured blockers before namespace assignment.
expected_result: The no-active-blocker sentinel remains visible only in legacy sentinel governance and never becomes an external graph endpoint or disconnected detail node.
actual_result: Scalar and global structured sentinel rows are excluded from external target collection while the scalar legacy sentinel remains classified in no_active_blocker_sentinels.
component: "SDK dependency governance, external resolver hooks, next, validate, and CLI adapters"
customer_impact: External dependencies silently park actionable work forever while the primary remediation can destroy the only machine-readable explanation.
