comments[24]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T21:25:57.770Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: complete all-status strict read covered 2593 readable items with no omissions. Closed pm-6sc8jq owns truthful stale-lifecycle governance for external blockers while pm-p9sc owns local dangling projections and pm-uxkf owns edge-aware blocked reads. No open item owns re-resolution plus safe validation classification. This recurrence is canonical for GitHub 1146 and 1147."
  "2026-08-28T21:26:39.465Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage evidence: issues #1146 and #1147 both point to this canonical combined external-blocker lifecycle and validation item at its merge-stable main-branch toon path."
  "2026-08-28T23:24:21.263Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: external classification, graph, actionability, next, and validation regressions passed; packed Node and Bun SDK consumers imported the public classifier successfully; full coverage passed exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-29T00:14:46.009Z","harness:codex","Final verification evidence: linked acceptance passed 9/9; the complete repository suite passed 586/586 files and 8100/8100 tests; exact coverage passed 60114/60114 statements, 45310/45310 branches, 12497/12497 functions, and 57886/57886 lines; repository static quality, command grammar, MCP parity, defect evidence, duplication, docs links, secret scan, and packed npm+Bun acceptance all passed."
  "2026-08-29T02:22:15.295Z","harness:codex","Review-round evidence: external locators preserve provider-specific case, structured locators become graph nodes even without source_kind, and stale resolver disposers cannot delete a replacement registration. The actionability, graph, validation, resolver, packed Node SDK, and packed Bun SDK paths pass."
  "2026-08-29T03:05:21.328Z","harness:codex","Second review-round evidence: explicit global/external source_kind metadata now preserves non-locator external blockers and projects them into actionability context; the shared classifier has one core owner and the public SDK re-exports it. Resolver supports exceptions fail closed without invoking resolve. Focused actionability/resolver regressions and the complete 8,108-test exact-coverage gate pass."
  "2026-08-29T03:06:04.567Z","harness:codex","Linked acceptance: pm test-all passed all four active items with zero failures; the shared connected regression command executed once for all duplicate-linked owners."
  "2026-08-29T04:41:15.752Z","harness:codex","Review-round findings: CodeRabbit and Greptile exact-head review identified local/external identifier collisions and an unsupported external-parent bypass. Reopened to keep edge provenance namespace-safe and parent validation truthful."
  "2026-08-29T05:25:25.570Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: explicit external PM-42 remains external even beside closed local pm-42; graph nodes use provenance-selected external:PM-42 identity; locator-shaped parents remain subject to local dangling validation. Connected and focused graph suites passed, exact repository coverage is literal 100/100/100/100, and the packed Bun SDK import succeeded."
  "2026-08-29T06:08:47.850Z","harness:codex","Final CodeRabbit review findings: actionability corpus indexing can collapse case-distinct or local/external blockers in a lowercase keyspace, and a synchronous resolver throw can abort Promise.allSettled setup before later resolvers run. Reopened for provenance-qualified keying and promise-boundary isolation."
  "2026-08-29T06:28:55.117Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: blocker de-duplication now uses provenance-qualified keys, preserves explicit external case, and isolates synchronous resolver throws without preventing later resolvers. Focused regressions, full 8,112-test exact coverage, quality:static, and linked acceptance passed."
  "2026-08-29T07:13:40.052Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit exact-head finding: graph assembly still lowercases external target keys, collapsing case-distinct provider locators despite actionability preserving them. Reopened for graph-wide identity parity."
  "2026-08-29T07:43:03.256Z","harness:codex","Review closure evidence: external locator identity is now case-preserving through endpoint collection, graph lookup, duplicate-row classification, and ordering-contradiction classification while local PM ids remain case-folded. Case-distinct scalar and structured Jira locators create separate nodes; graph regressions and full exact coverage pass."
  "2026-08-29T08:19:32.136Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit exact-head finding: external blocked_by dependency projection trims id without validating its decoded runtime type, so a malformed package payload can abort corpus actionability. Reopened for fail-closed row skipping."
  "2026-08-29T08:23:18.382Z","harness:codex","TDD review fix: added a malformed decoded external blocker dependency ([shell-expansion-redacted] absent at runtime), reproduced the  crash, then guarded the structured external-id projection. Focused actionability and context-integrity suites pass."
  "2026-08-29T08:23:27.184Z","harness:codex","Correction to the immediately preceding shell-mangled evidence: the malformed decoded dependency had a missing runtime id field, and the reproduced failure was an unsafe trim call. The structured external-id projection now validates that id is a nonblank string before normalization."
  "2026-08-29T08:44:03.462Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: strict static quality passed; full suite passed 586 files and 8,115 tests with exact coverage statements 60,145/60,145, branches 45,366/45,366, functions 12,508/12,508, lines 57,915/57,915. Linked PM acceptance passed the external graph/provenance and malformed actionability regressions with zero failures."
  "2026-08-29T09:36:40.857Z","harness:codex","TDD review evidence: registering a class-instance resolver lost prototype methods under object spread and returned null. Registration now wraps supports/resolve while preserving receiver binding and the normalized public name. Focused green: 4 files, 115/115 tests."
  "2026-08-29T09:58:28.812Z","harness:codex","Verification: exact repository coverage passed at 100/100/100/100. PM acceptance ran all 3 linked entries, covering 14, 28, and 35 tests respectively; all passed with zero failure categories. Static, contract, and assurance gates passed."
  "2026-08-29T10:42:49.670Z","harness:codex","TDD review evidence: supporting providers that fulfilled with undefined or a non-string optional field crashed resolution before a later valid provider could run. The new regressions fail on the unsafe status/trim access; the SDK now validates the runtime result object, required status, and optional string fields before projection."
  "2026-08-29T10:58:53.788Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: linked acceptance passed 3/3 commands with 79 assertions across context integrity, dependency provenance, graph governance, and actionability suites. Full repository coverage passed 586 files and 8,119 tests at exact 100/100/100/100. Focused ESLint and every TypeScript project passed; static quality, security, and dependency audit passed."
  "2026-08-29T11:49:59.815Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit exact-head finding: external target collection uses reference normalization instead of graph normalization, allowing a global no-active-blocker sentinel to enter the external node namespace even though edge normalization drops it. Adding scalar and structured negative controls before implementation."
  "2026-08-29T12:24:41.994Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: scalar and global structured no-active-blocker rows reproduced an unwanted fifth external endpoint. Graph-target normalization now excludes both before namespace allocation while retaining the scalar row in legacy sentinel governance. Focused graph and connected suites passed; full repository rerun passed 586 files and 8,120 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-08-29T12:50:12.982Z","harness:codex","Final closure evidence: sentinel normalization excludes scalar and structured no-active-blocker markers before external namespace allocation while preserving legacy sentinel reporting. Linked acceptance passed 3/3 commands (79 assertions), repository coverage passed 8,121/8,121 at exact 100/100/100/100, and the full static assurance pipeline passed."
learnings[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T23:24:37.448Z","harness:codex","A syntactically valid remote locator is a typed graph node even when no resolver is installed. Unknown external state must remain explicit evidence, never be rewritten as local dangling corruption."
  "2026-08-29T00:14:46.442Z","harness:codex","Provider integrations belong behind the SDK resolver registry: core classifies and preserves external identity while bounded package-owned providers supply lifecycle evidence. Resolver failures and absent providers fail closed to explicit unknown state instead of deleting context."
  "2026-08-29T05:25:26.063Z","harness:codex","Dependency identity is provenance plus normalized identifier: spelling alone cannot decide whether a target belongs to the canonical local namespace or the external namespace."
  "2026-08-29T06:28:54.520Z","harness:codex",Dependency identity includes provenance and external case semantics; local canonicalization must never collapse distinct external references. Resolver isolation must also defer invocation so synchronous throws become settled failures.
  "2026-08-29T07:43:03.728Z","harness:codex","Reference identity must include its namespace: local item ids use case-insensitive canonicalization, while external locators preserve exact case and must never share a folded key."
  "2026-08-29T08:44:03.888Z","harness:codex",Decoded tracker metadata remains an untrusted runtime boundary even when TypeScript declares a string field; dependency projections must validate scalar types before trimming or normalization.
